<ul class="enc-list"><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/o-ceallaigh"><span class="enc-name">Ó Ceallaigh</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The Ó Ceallaigh, or O'Kellys, were the ruling family of Uí Maine in east Galway and south Roscommon from the 10th century to the 16th.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/o-cleirigh"><span class="enc-name">Ó Cléirigh</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The Ó Cléirigh, or O'Clerys, were a learned family of historians and poets in the service of the O'Donnell lords of Tír Chonaill.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/o-raghallaigh"><span class="enc-name">Ó Raghallaigh</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The Ó Raghallaigh, or O'Reillys, were a Gaelic Irish dynasty of the Uí Briúin Bréifne who ruled East Breifne, roughly modern County Cavan, from the 13th to the late…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/o-ruairc"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/o-ruairc.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ó Ruairc</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The Ó Ruairc, or O'Rourkes, were a Gaelic Irish dynasty of the Uí Briúin Bréifne who ruled Breifne from the 10th century and, after the kingdom split in 1256, West…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/obrien-dynasty"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/obrien-dynasty.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">O'Brien dynasty</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The O'Brien dynasty, in Irish Uí Briain, was a royal family of Munster descended from Brian Boru of the Dál gCais.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ocahan-dynasty"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ocahan-dynasty.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">O'Cahan dynasty</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The O'Cahans, Ó Catháin, were a Gaelic ruling family in the north of present-day County Londonderry, Ireland, from the 12th century to the early 17th.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/ocarrolls-of-ely"><span class="enc-name">O'Carrolls of Ely</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The O'Carrolls (Ua Cerbaill) of Ely were the ruling dynasty of Éile in the Irish midlands from the 11th century, giving their name to the territory of Ely O'Carroll.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/oconnor-faly"><span class="enc-name">O'Connor Faly</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The O'Connors Faly, Ua Conchobair Failge, were the ruling family of Uí Failge in the Irish midlands from the 11th century to the 1550s.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/oconnor-kerry"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/oconnor-kerry.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">O'Connor Kerry</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The O'Connor Kerry, in Irish Ó Conchobhair Chiarraí, were the ruling family of the Ciarraige Luachra in north Kerry, Ireland, from the 11th century.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/oconnor-sligo"><span class="enc-name">O'Connor Sligo</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">O'Connor Sligo was a branch of the royal O'Connor dynasty of Connacht, descended from Brian Luighnech, which ruled Lower Connacht from Sligo Castle.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/odonnell-dynasty"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/odonnell-dynasty.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">O'Donnell dynasty</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The O'Donnells, Ó Domhnaill, were a branch of the Cenél Conaill who ruled Tír Chonaill in north-western Ireland from the 13th century to 1607.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/odonovan-family"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/odonovan-family.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">O'Donovan family</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The O'Donovans, in Irish Ó Donnabháin, are an Irish family descended from Donnubán mac Cathail, a 10th-century king of the Uí Fidgenti in County Limerick.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/odriscoll"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/odriscoll.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">O'Driscoll</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The O'Driscolls (Ó hEidirsceoil) were a Gaelic Irish family of south-west Cork and the ruling line of the Corcu Loígde, named after an early medieval ancestor called…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ofarrell"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ofarrell.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">O'Farrell</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The O'Farrells were an Irish ruling family who held the lordship of Annaly, in what became County Longford, from the 12th century.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/oflaherty"><span class="enc-name">O'Flaherty</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The O'Flahertys, Ó Flaithbheartaigh, are a Gaelic Irish family who were originally kings of Muintir Murchada east of Lough Corrib in Connacht.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/omalley-clan"><span class="enc-name">O'Malley clan</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The O'Malleys (Ó Máille) were a Gaelic seafaring lineage of Umall, around Clew Bay in County Mayo, western Ireland.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/omore"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/omore.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">O'More</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The O'Mores, Irish Ó Mórdha, were the ruling family of the Loígis in the Irish midlands from the 11th century, taking their name from an ancestor called Mórda.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/o-neill-dynasty"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/o-neill-dynasty.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">O'Neill dynasty</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The O'Neill dynasty, Ua Néill in Irish, was a branch of the Cenél nEógain of the northern Uí Néill, named after Niall Glúndub, a high king killed in 919.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/osullivan-dynasty"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/osullivan-dynasty.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">O'Sullivan dynasty</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The O'Sullivans (Ó Súilleabháin) were a Gaelic Irish family of the Eóganachta of Munster who, after the Anglo-Norman invasion, settled in south Kerry and west Cork.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/oath-of-pontida"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/oath-of-pontida.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Oath of Pontida</span><span class="enc-type">Event</span><span class="enc-snip">The Oath of Po